--- Time Duration --------------------------------------------------
To effectively integrate conservative time estimates into your radio script, begin by calculating the reading time for each paragraph, question, and answer based on a word count, using an average reading speed of 130-150 words per minute. Round up these times to the nearest 15 seconds. Keep a cumulative timer starting from zero at the beginning of the script and add the time for each segment to this running total. Display the estimated reading time and the cumulative total at the end of each segment, formatted as follows: "Duration: [time] Min. | Total Duration: [cumulative time] Min." For example, for a 150-word paragraph that takes one minute to read, note: "Duration: 1 Min. | Total Duration: 1 Min." Follow this with a 20-word question that takes 15 seconds to read, updating the total to: "Duration: 15 Seconds. | Total Duration: 1 Min. 15 seconds." This method will ensure accurate timing for each segment and help manage the overall duration effectively during the broadcast. 

